{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 74,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O God, why hast thou cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " off for ever?\nWhy doth thine anger smoke against the sheep of thy pasture?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember thy congregation, which thou hast gotten of old,\nWhich thou hast redeemed to be the tribe of thine inheritance;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mount Zion, wherein thou hast dwelt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lift up thy feet unto the perpetual ruins,All the evil that the enemy hath done in the sanctuary.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thine adversaries have roared in the midst of thine assembly;\nThey have set up their ensigns for signs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They seemed as men that lifted up\nAxes upon a thicket of trees.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now all the carved work thereof\nThey break down with hatchet and hammers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have set thy sanctuary on fire;\nThey have profaned the dwelling-place of thy name ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "by casting it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They said in their heart, Let us make havoc of them altogether:\nThey have burned up all the synagogues of God in the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We see not our signs:\nThere is no more any prophet;\nNeither is there among us any that knoweth how long.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long, O God, shall the adversary reproach?\nShall the enemy blaspheme thy name for ever?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why drawest thou back thy hand, even thy right hand?",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pluck it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out of thy bosom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " consume ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet God is my King of old,\nWorking salvation in the midst of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou didst divide the sea by thy strength:\nThou brakest the heads of the sea-monsters in the waters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou brakest the heads of leviathan in pieces;\nThou gavest him to be food to the people inhabiting the wilderness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou didst cleave fountain and flood:\nThou driedst up mighty rivers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The day is thine, the night also is thine:\nThou hast prepared the light and the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast set all the borders of the earth:\nThou hast made summer and winter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember this, that the enemy hath reproached, O Jehovah,\nAnd that a foolish people hath blasphemed thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh deliver not the soul of thy turtle-dove unto the wild beast:\nForget not the life of thy poor for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have respect unto the covenant;\nFor the dark places of the earth are full of the habitations of violence.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh let not the oppressed return ashamed:\nLet the poor and needy praise thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise, O God, plead thine own cause:\nRemember how the foolish man reproacheth thee all the day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.74.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Forget not the voice of thine adversaries:\nThe tumult of those that rise up against thee ascendeth continually.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "A complaint over the devastation of the land by the enemy.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "Maschil of Asaph.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
